WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:09.775
Last week was my birthday.

2
00:00:10.555 --> 00:00:14.057
My parents gave me a cool gift—my own smartphone.

3
00:00:17.438 --> 00:00:19.039
"Enjoying your new phone, Ella?"

4
00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.099
Dad asked.

5
00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:23.120
"Don't forget your online manners.

6
00:00:23.141 --> 00:00:27.802
"Number one: Think before you send or post."

7
00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:33.244
I groaned as Dad started listing our family's "netiquette rules."

8
00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:44.347
"Two: Never chat or share pictures with strangers By now I'd heard these rules a million times.

9
00:00:45.268 --> 00:00:48.609
While Dad continued reciting them, I looked down at my phone.

10
00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:52.089
I had a new message from my friend, Josh.

11
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:53.670
Josh: Hey!

12
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.770
Still want to go to the movies tomorrow?

13
00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.011
Ella: Yes!

14
00:00:58.111 --> 00:01:00.012
Josh: Great!

15
00:01:00.612 --> 00:01:03.453
Violet? I rolled my eyes.

16
00:01:06.115 --> 00:01:09.137
Josh, Violet, and I had been friends since third grade.

17
00:01:10.077 --> 00:01:12.799
But things started to change when we entered middle school.

18
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.462
Violet had joined the drama club and made new friends.

19
00:01:17.562 --> 00:01:22.125
Now whenever she hung around with us, she sang songs from musicals—loudly.

20
00:01:22.886 --> 00:01:23.987
It got on my nerves.

21
00:01:25.288 --> 00:01:27.849
"Ella?" "Oops, sorry, Dad.

22
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.550
Josh asked me something."

23
00:01:30.911 --> 00:01:31.632
He frowned.

24
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.623
"Dad, you don't have to tell me about netiquette again," I said quickly.

25
00:01:36.643 --> 00:01:40.186
"Trust me—I know all the rules already."

26
00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:42.448
"Good." He nodded.

27
00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:48.413
"Then it's time to follow rule number five: no screen time until your chores are done."

28
00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:50.735
I saluted him.

29
00:01:50.755 --> 00:01:51.656
"Got it."

30
00:01:57.761 --> 00:01:59.122
Ella: No Violet tomorrow.

31
00:01:59.603 --> 00:02:00.944
I'm sick of her loud singing!

32
00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:08.143
I inserted an emoticon with a person plugging her ears, and then I went to fold laundry.

33
00:02:09.043 --> 00:02:12.525
The next day when I met Josh at the movie theater, he rushed up to me.

34
00:02:12.545 --> 00:02:15.887
"So, is Violet really angry?"

35
00:02:15.907 --> 00:02:18.409
"Angry about what?"

36
00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:19.389
I asked.

37
00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.051
"About what you said about her."

38
00:02:22.071 --> 00:02:24.572
"I don't know what you're talking about."

39
00:02:25.933 --> 00:02:27.033
Josh looked worried.

40
00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:31.696
"Yesterday when we were talking, it was a group chat."

41
00:02:32.764 --> 00:02:33.464
I blinked.

42
00:02:34.184 --> 00:02:38.846
"Does that mean "Yep, Violet was in our chat too."

43
00:02:48.808 --> 00:02:50.749
Josh and I bought tickets and sat down.

44
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.251
He started laughing at something on his phone, but I was too anxious to laugh at anything.

45
00:02:59.291 --> 00:03:01.512
I was thinking about how I'd insulted Violet.

46
00:03:03.136 --> 00:03:04.277
No Violet tomorrow.

47
00:03:04.858 --> 00:03:06.339
I'm sick of her loud singing!

48
00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.540
I felt terrible.

49
00:03:09.261 --> 00:03:12.543
Violet and I had grown apart, but she was still my friend.

50
00:03:12.563 --> 00:03:17.987
"Rule number one," I thought as tears slipped down my cheeks.

51
00:03:18.007 --> 00:03:20.649
"Think before you send."

52
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.352
After the movie I biked over to Violet’s house.

53
00:03:35.568 --> 00:03:37.489
"I'm sorry, Violet," I blurted out.

54
00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:44.090
"I didn't realize it was a group chat and I kept talking, desperately trying to apologize.

55
00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.251
Violet looked away.

56
00:03:46.271 --> 00:03:48.051
"It's okay."

57
00:03:49.412 --> 00:03:50.132
I shook my head.

58
00:03:50.152 --> 00:03:52.292
"No, it's not."

59
00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:57.474
We stood in silence for a few moments, and then Violet looked up.

60
00:03:57.494 --> 00:04:00.715
"You definitely hurt my feelings, Ella.

61
00:04:01.835 --> 00:04:05.356
But my family says I do talk about theater stuff too much."

62
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.220
She flashed a weak smile at me.

63
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.482
"I'll try to stop singing show tunes, I promise."

64
00:04:13.502 --> 00:04:17.683
"I made such a stupid mistake," I mumbled.

65
00:04:19.103 --> 00:04:19.944
Violet nodded.

66
00:04:19.964 --> 00:04:23.645
"My parents always say to be cautious online.

67
00:04:24.725 --> 00:04:27.706
You can't take something back once you send it or post it."

68
00:04:28.746 --> 00:04:29.486
I swallowed.

69
00:04:30.867 --> 00:04:32.567
I'd learned that lesson the hard way.

70
00:04:33.927 --> 00:04:36.028
She shrugged and opened the door wider.

71
00:04:37.284 --> 00:04:38.466
"Want to come in for a while?"

72
00:04:38.486 --> 00:04:43.851
"Sure." I turned off my phone and then went inside.
